<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Red Flag</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1889">1889</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Irishman Jim Connell wrote &quot;The Red Flag&quot; in 1889 in Nicholas Donovan's house: six stanzas, each followed by a chorus, praising the sacrifices and solidarity of the international labour movement.</p></div>
